{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":426743,"ns":0,"title":"Graph coloring","extract":"In graph theory, graph coloring is a methodic assignment of labels traditionally called \"colors\" to elements of a graph. The assignment is subject to certain constraints, such as that no two adjacent elements have the same color.","description":"Methodic assignment of colors to elements of a graph","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}